 "Let's sketch the graph of $y=f(x)=5sin⁡(2x).$\n\n![](images/67/67f6ec4f72e7bd74ac9ae5fa0f195cda1e90e8d8e6fad1bf85944a3dfd17fdfb.png)\n\nAs $x$ increases to $\\infty $, the graph oscillates between the values $y=-5$ and $y=5$ indefinitely. Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\lim_{x\\to \\,\\infty }f(x)=\\lim_{x\\to \\,\\infty }5sin⁡(2x)=DNE.\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186235424 :question/problem "![](images/47/47553a1d2bcd37d3040bf96c0fc0446b81404a07ab931e457788e62d86dee234.png)     \n                                \n                            \n\n   \n\nThe graph of the function $g(h)$ is shown above, where\n\n$$\ng(h)=\\frac{5}{h}sin⁡(\\pi +2h).\n$$\n\nFrom the graph, what is ${lim}_{h\\to \\,0}g(h)?$ If the limit does not exist, write \"DNE\" (without the quotation marks).\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n${lim}_{h\\to \\,0}g(h)=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n{{field-1}}" "![](images/47/47553a1d2bcd37d3040bf96c0fc0446b81404a07ab931e457788e62d86dee234.png)     \n                                \n                            \n\n   \n\nThe graph of the function $g(h)$ is shown above, where\n\n$$\ng(h)=\\frac{5}{h}sin⁡(\\pi +2h).\n$$\n\nFrom the graph, what is $\\lim_{h\\to \\,0}g(h)?$ If the limit does not exist, write \"DNE\" (without the quotation marks).\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n       