[\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(2+\\frac{i}{n})\\cdot \\frac{2}{n}]"] [:db/cas 17592186248658 :answer/value "{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}[\\sqrt{\\frac{i}{n}}\\cdot \\frac{5}{n}]" "\\lim_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}[\\sqrt{\\frac{i}{n}}\\cdot \\frac{5}{n}]"] [:db/cas 17592186248687 :answer/value "{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}[\\sqrt{\\frac{i}{n}}\\cdot \\frac{4}{n}]" "\\lim_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}[\\sqrt{\\frac{i}{n}}\\cdot \\frac{4}{n}]"] [:db/cas 17592186248762 :answer/value "{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{k=1}^{n}[\\sqrt{9+\\frac{4k}{n}}\\cdot \\frac{4}{n}]" "\\lim_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{k=1}^{n}[\\sqrt{9+\\frac{4k}{n}}\\cdot \\frac{4}{n}]"] [:db/cas 17592186248830 :answer/value "{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{k=1}^{n}[\\sqrt{1+\\frac{5k}{n}}\\cdot \\frac{5}{n}]" "\\lim_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{k=1}^{n}[\\sqrt{1+\\frac{5k}{n}}\\cdot \\frac{5}{n}]"] [:db/cas 17592186249075 :answer/value "{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}[\\sqrt{\\frac{2i}{n}}\\cdot \\frac{4}{n}]" "\\lim_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}[\\sqrt{\\frac{2i}{n}}\\cdot \\frac{4}{n}]"] [:db/cas 17592186249122 :answer/value "{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}[{e}^{4i/n}\\cdot \\frac{4}{n}]" "\\lim_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}[{e}^{4i/n}\\cdot \\frac{4}{n}]"] [:db/cas 17592186249147 :answer/value "{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{k=1}^{n}[\\sqrt{4+\\frac{5k}{n}}\\cdot \\frac{9}{n}]" "\\lim_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{k=1}^{n}[\\sqrt{4+\\frac{5k}{n}}\\cdot \\frac{9}{n}]"] [:db/cas 17592186249155 :answer/value "{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}[\\operatorname{arctan}⁡\\left(\\frac{i}{n}\\right)\\cdot \\frac{4}{n}]" "\\lim_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}[\\operatorname{arctan}⁡\\left(\\frac{i}{n}\\right)\\cdot \\frac{4}{n}]"] [:db/cas 17592186249445 :answer/value "{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}[{e}^{5i/n}\\cdot \\frac{5}{n}]" "\\lim_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}[{e}^{5i/n}\\cdot \\frac{5}{n}]"] [:db/cas 17592186249614 :answer/value "{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}[{e}^{5i/n}\\cdot \\frac{4}{n}]" "\\lim_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}[{e}^{5i/n}\\cdot \\frac{4}{n}]"] [:db/cas 17592186249655 :answer/value "{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}[\\operatorname{arctan}⁡\\left(\\frac{i}{n}\\right)\\cdot \\frac{1}{n}]" "\\lim_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}[\\operatorname{arctan}⁡\\left(\\frac{i}{n}\\right)\\cdot \\frac{1}{n}]"] [:db/cas 17592186250137 :question/problem "Find the function $f(x)$ and the value of $b,$ given that $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{0}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{k=0}^{n-1}[\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{2k}{n}\\right)\\cdot \\frac{2}{n}].\n$$" "Find the function $f(x)$ and the value of $b,$ given that $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{0}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=\\lim_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{k=0}^{n-1}[\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{2k}{n}\\right)\\cdot \\frac{2}{n}].\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186250137 :question/worked-solution "A definite integral can be defined as the limit of a left Riemann sum as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{k=0}^{n-1}f({x}_{k})\\cdot Δx\n$$\n\nwhere $Δx=\\frac{b-a}{n}$ and ${x}_{k}=a+kΔx.$\n\nNotice that we're given that the lower limit $a=0.$ \n\nComparing the given summation with the general expression above, we see that $Δx=\\frac{2}{n}.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\n\\frac{2}{n}=\\frac{b-0}{n}\\,⟹\\,b=2.\n$$\n\nConsequently,  ${x}_{k}=\\frac{2k}{n}$ and $f({x}_{k})=\\operatorname{sin}⁡{x}_{k}.$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{k=0}^{n-1}[\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{2k}{n}\\right)\\cdot \\frac{2}{n}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $f(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x$ and $b=2.$" "A definite integral can be defined as the limit of a left Riemann sum as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=\\lim_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{k=0}^{n-1}f({x}_{k})\\cdot Δx\n$$\n\nwhere $Δx=\\frac{b-a}{n}$ and ${x}_{k}=a+kΔx.$\n\nNotice that we're given that the lower limit $a=0.$ \n\nComparing the given summation with the general expression above, we see that $Δx=\\frac{2}{n}.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\n\\frac{2}{n}=\\frac{b-0}{n}\\,⟹\\,b=2.\n$$\n\nConsequently,  ${x}_{k}=\\frac{2k}{n}$ and $f({x}_{k})=\\operatorname{sin}⁡{x}_{k}.$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x=\\lim_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{k=0}^{n-1}[\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{2k}{n}\\right)\\cdot \\frac{2}{n}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $f(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x$ and $b=2.$"] [:db/cas 17592186250207 :question/problem "${lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{e}^{-x}}=$" "$\\lim_{x\\to -\\infty }\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{e}^{-x}}=$"] [:db/cas 17592186250208 :question/problem "${lim}_{x\\to 1}\\frac{1-x+x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{{x}^{2}-2x+1}=$" "$\\lim_{x\\to 1}\\frac{1-x+x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{{x}^{2}-2x+1}=$"] [:db/cas 17592186250209 :question/problem "${lim}_{x\\to -1}\\frac{(x+2)\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+2)-x-1}{{x}^{2}+2x+1}=$" "$\\lim_{x\\to -1}\\frac{(x+2)\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+2)-x-1}{{x}^{2}+2x+1}=$"] [:db/cas 17592186250210 :question/problem "${lim}_{x\\to 1}\\frac{2+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi x)}{{x}^{2}-2x+1}=$" "$\\lim_{x\\to 1}\\frac{2+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi x)}{{x}^{2}-2x+1}=$"] [:db/cas 17592186250211 :question/problem "${lim}_{x\\to -1}\\frac{{x}^{2}+2x+1}{({x}^{2}-4)^{2}-12x-21}=$" "$\\lim_{x\\to -1}\\frac{{x}^{2}+2x+1}{({x}^{2}-4)^{2}-12x-21}=$"] [:db/cas 17592186250212 :question/problem "${lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{x{e}^{-x}-x+2{x}^{2}}{{sin}^{2}⁡x}=$" "$\\lim_{x\\to 0}\\frac{x{e}^{-x}-x+2{x}^{2}}{{sin}^{2}⁡x}=$"] [:db/cas 17592186250423 :question/problem "Evaluate ${lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4x}{x}.$" "Evaluate $\\lim_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4x}{x}.$"] [:db/cas 17592186250426 :question/problem "Evaluate ${lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1-x)-2x}{x+1}.$" "Evaluate $\\lim_{x\\to -\\infty }\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1-x)-2x}{x+1}.$"] [:db/cas 17592186250429 :question/problem "Evaluate ${lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{{x}^{2}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2x}.$" "Evaluate $\\lim_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{{x}^{2}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2x}.$"] [:db/cas 17592186250430 :question/problem "Evaluate ${lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{\\sqrt{x}}{{ln}^{2}⁡x}.$" "Evaluate $\\lim_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{\\sqrt{x}}{{ln}^{2}⁡x}.$"] [:db/cas 17592186253449 :question/problem "${lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{(1+\\frac{1}{n})}^{n/3}=$" "$$\n\\lim_{n\\to \\infty }{(1+\\frac{1}{n})}^{n/3}=\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186253451 :question/problem "${lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{(1+\\frac{1}{n})}^{20nx}=$" "$$\n\\lim_{n\\to \\infty }{(1+\\frac{1}{n})}^{20nx}=\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186253453 :question/problem "${lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{(1+\\frac{1}{n})}^{nxy}=$" "$$\n\\lim_{n\\to \\infty }{(1+\\frac{1}{n})}^{nxy}=\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186253455 :question/problem "${lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{(1+\\frac{z}{n})}^{\\pi n}=$" "$$\n\\lim_{n\\to \\infty }{(1+\\frac{z}{n})}^{\\pi n}=\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186253460 :question/problem "${lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{(1+\\frac{x}{n})}^{-6n}=$" "$$\n\\lim_{n\\to \\infty }{(1+\\frac{x}{n})}^{-6n}=\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186253461 :question/problem "${lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{(1+\\frac{x}{n})}^{n{y}^{2}}=$" "$$\n\\lim_{n\\to \\infty }{(1+\\frac{x}{n})}^{n{y}^{2}}=\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186259538 :question/worked-solution "Recall that for large values of $n,$ we have\n\n$$\nn!≫{e}^{n}≫{n}^{m}≫\\operatorname{ln}⁡(n),\n$$\n\nwhere $≫$ means \"much greater than,\" and $m>0.$\n\nWe calculate the limit of the sequence as $n$ approaches infinity:\n\n$$\n{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{a}_{n}={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }(\\frac{{n}^{2}}{{e}^{n/2}}-1)=-1+{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }\\frac{{n}^{2}}{{e}^{n/2}}\n$$\n\nBoth the numerator and denominator approach infinity as $n\\to \\infty .$ However, the denominator is growing much faster than the numerator, and we conclude that\n\n$$\n{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }\\frac{{n}^{2}}{{e}^{n