}{h}\\right).\n$$\n\nSince $f(x)={2}^{x+2y},$  we have that \n\n$$\nf(x+h,y)={2}^{x+h+2y}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=\\lim_{h\\to 0}\\left(\\frac{{2}^{x+h+2y}-{2}^{x+2y}}{h}\\right).\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186278230 :question/worked-solution "The partial derivative of $f$ with respect to $x$ is given by the limit \n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂x}={lim}_{h\\to 0}\\left(\\frac{f(x+h,y)-f(x,y)}{h}\\right).\n$$\n\nSince $f(x)=\\operatorname{log}⁡(x+3y),$  we have that \n\n$$\nf(x+h,y)=\\operatorname{log}⁡(x+h+3y).\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂x}={lim}_{h\\to 0}\\left(\\frac{\\operatorname{log}⁡(x+h+3y)-\\operatorname{log}⁡(x+3y)}{h}\\right).\n$$" "The partial derivative of $f$ with respect to $x$ is given by the limit \n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=\\lim_{h\\to 0}\\left(\\frac{f(x+h,y)-f(x,y)}{h}\\right).\n$$\n\nSince $f(x)=\\operatorname{log}⁡(x+3y),$  we have that \n\n$$\nf(x+h,y)=\\operatorname{log}⁡(x+h+3y).\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=\\lim_{h\\to 0}\\left(\\frac{\\operatorname{log}⁡(x+h+3y)-\\operatorname{log}⁡(x+3y)}{h}\\right).\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186278232 :question/worked-solution "The derivative of $f$ with respect to $y$ is given by the limit \n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂y}={lim}_{h\\to 0}\\left(\\frac{f(x,y+h)-f(x,y)}{h}\\right).\n$$\n\nSince $f(x)=\\frac{{x}^{2}}{(y+2)^{3}},$  we have that \n\n$$\nf(x,y+h)=\\frac{{x}^{2}}{(y+h+2)^{3}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂y}={lim}_{h\\to 0}[\\frac{1}{h}(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{(y+h+2)^{3}}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{(y+2)^{3}})].\n$$" "The derivative of $f$ with respect to $y$ is given by the limit \n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=\\lim_{h\\to 0}\\left(\\frac{f(x,y+h)-f(x,y)}{h}\\right).\n$$\n\nSince $f(x)=\\frac{{x}^{2}}{(y+2)^{3}},$  we have that \n\n$$\nf(x,y+h)=\\frac{{x}^{2}}{(y+h+2)^{3}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=\\lim_{h\\to 0}[\\frac{1}{h}(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{(y+h+2)^{3}}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{(y+2)^{3}})].\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186278233 :question/worked-solution "The derivative of $f$ with respect to $y$ is given by the limit \n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂y}={lim}_{h\\to 0}\\left(\\frac{f(x,y+h)-f(x,y)}{h}\\right).\n$$\n\nSince $f(x)={3}^{xy},$  we have that \n\n$$\nf(x,y+h)={3}^{x(y+h)}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂y}={lim}_{h\\to 0}\\left(\\frac{{3}^{x(y+h)}-{3}^{xy}}{h}\\right).\n$$" "The derivative of $f$ with respect to $y$ is given by the limit \n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=\\lim_{h\\to 0}\\left(\\frac{f(x,y+h)-f(x,y)}{h}\\right).\n$$\n\nSince $f(x)={3}^{xy},$  we have that \n\n$$\nf(x,y+h)={3}^{x(y+h)}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=\\lim_{h\\to 0}\\left(\\frac{{3}^{x(y+h)}-{3}^{xy}}{h}\\right).\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186278234 :question/worked-solution "The derivative of $f$ with respect to $y$ is given by the limit \n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂y}={lim}_{h\\to 0}\\left(\\frac{f(x,y+h)-f(x,y)}{h}\\right).\n$$\n\nSince $f(x)=\\sqrt[3]{{x}^{2}-y},$  we have that \n\n$$\nf(x,y+h)=\\sqrt[3]{{x}^{2}-(y+h)}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂y}={lim}_{h\\to 0}\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt[3]{{x}^{2}-(y+h)}-\\sqrt[3]{{x}^{2}-y}}{h}\\right).\n$$" "The derivative of $f$ with respect to $y$ is given by the limit \n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=\\lim_{h\\to 0}\\left(\\frac{f(x,y+h)-f(x,y)}{h}\\right).\n$$\n\nSince $f(x)=\\sqrt[3]{{x}^{2}-y},$  we have that \n\n$$\nf(x,y+h)=\\sqrt[3]{{x}^{2}-(y+h)}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=\\lim_{h\\to 0}\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt[3]{{x}^{2}-(y+h)}-\\sqrt[3]{{x}^{2}-y}}{h}\\right).\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186297260 :question/problem "${lim}_{x\\to \\infty }(13{x}^{13})=${{field-1}}" "$\\lim_{x\\to \\infty }(13{x}^{13})=${{field-1}}"] [:db/cas 17592186297261 :question/problem "If $p(x)=-3{x}^{5}$ and $q(x)=\\frac{4}{{x}^{7}}$, then\n\n${lim}_{x\\to \\infty }({x}^{2}\\cdot p(x)\\cdot q(x))=$\n{{field-1}}." "If $p(x)=-3{x}^{5}$ and $q(x)=\\frac{4}{{x}^{7}}$, then\n\n$$\n\\lim_{x\\to \\infty }({x}^{2}\\cdot p(x)\\cdot q(x))=\n$$\n{{field-1}}."] [:db/cas 17592186297262 :question/problem "If $p(x)=10{x}^{8}$ and $q(x)=2{x}^{8},$ then\n\n${lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{p(x)}{q(x