 \\,1}\\sqrt{\\frac{3f(x)-g(x)}{f(x)}}=$\n{{field-1}}" "![](images/52/52c11d9ff3afeef74c579d4cb2c5448c9f5b77b7d6569535214bb67408276026.png)\n\nIf the figure above shows the graph of the functions $f(x)$ and $g(x),$ then\n\n$$\n\\lim_{x\\to \\,1}\\sqrt{\\frac{3f(x)-g(x)}{f(x)}}=\n$$\n{{field-1}}"] [:db/cas 17592186311948 :question/problem "Evaluate the following limit:\n\n${lim}_{x\\to 5}\\frac{5-\\sqrt{5x}}{5-x}=$\n{{field-1}}" "Evaluate the following limit:\n\n$$\n\\lim_{x\\to 5}\\frac{5-\\sqrt{5x}}{5-x}=\n$$\n{{field-1}}"] [:db/cas 17592186311949 :question/problem "Evaluate the following limit:\n\n${lim}_{x\\to 8}\\frac{8-\\sqrt{8x}}{x-8}=$\n{{field-1}}" "Evaluate the following limit:\n\n$$\n\\lim_{x\\to 8}\\frac{8-\\sqrt{8x}}{x-8}=\n$$\n{{field-1}}"] [:db/cas 17592186311950 :question/problem "Evaluate the following limit:\n\n${lim}_{x\\to 3}\\frac{\\sqrt{x+1}-2}{{x}^{2}-x-6}=$\n{{field-1}}" "Evaluate the following limit:\n\n$\\lim_{x\\to 3}\\frac{\\sqrt{x+1}-2}{{x}^{2}-x-6}=$\n{{field-1}}"] [:db/cas 17592186311952 :question/problem "Evaluate the following limit:\n\n${lim}_{x\\to (1/4)}\\frac{4x-1}{2x-\\sqrt{x}}=$\n{{field-1}}" "Evaluate the following limit:\n\n$$\n\\lim_{x\\to (1/4)}\\frac{4x-1}{2x-\\sqrt{x}}=\n$$\n{{field-1}}"] [:db/cas 17592186311953 :question/problem "Evaluate the following limit:\n\n${lim}_{x\\to 64}\\frac{x-64}{\\sqrt{4x}-16}=$\n{{field-1}}" "Evaluate the following limit:\n\n$$\n\\lim_{x\\to 64}\\frac{x-64}{\\sqrt{4x}-16}=\n$$\n{{field-1}}"] [:db/cas 17592186311954 :question/problem "Evaluate the following limit:\n\n${lim}_{x\\to 3}\\frac{x-3}{3x-\\sqrt{27x}}=$\n{{field-1}}" "Evaluate the following limit:\n\n$$\n\\lim_{x\\to 3}\\frac{x-3}{3x-\\sqrt{27x}}=\n$$\n{{field-1}}"] [:db/cas 17592186311958 :question/problem "Evaluate the following limit:\n\n${lim}_{z\\to 6}\\frac{z-6}{\\sqrt{3z-2}-4}=$\n{{field-1}}" "Evaluate the following limit:\n\n$$\n\\lim_{z\\to 6}\\frac{z-6}{\\sqrt{3z-2}-4}=\n$$\n{{field-1}}"] [:db/cas 17592186314717 :question/problem "Evaluate the following limit:\n\n${lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{{x}^{2}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5x)}=$\n{{field-1}}" "Evaluate the following limit:\n\n$\\lim_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{{x}^{2}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5x)}=$\n{{field-1}}"] [:db/cas 17592186314717 :question/worked-solution "Both the numerator and denominator approach $\\infty $ as $x\\to \\infty .$ However, since ${x}^{2}≫\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5x)$ for large values of $x,$ the numerator is growing much faster than the denominator. Consequently, we conclude that\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{{x}^{2}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5x)}=\\infty .\n$$" "Both the numerator and denominator approach $\\infty $ as $x\\to \\infty .$ However, since ${x}^{2}≫\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5x)$ for large values of $x,$ the numerator is growing much faster than the denominator. Consequently, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\lim_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{{x}^{2}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5x)}=\\infty .\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186314718 :question/problem "Evaluate the following limit:\n\n${lim}_{x\\to \\infty }(\\frac{{e}^{x}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}+2)=$\n{{field-1}}" "Evaluate the following limit:\n\n$\\lim_{x\\to \\infty }(\\frac{{e}^{x}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}+2)=$\n{{field-1}}"] [:db/cas 17592186314718 :question/worked-solution "Both the numerator and denominator approach $\\infty $ as $x\\to \\infty .$ However, since ${e}^{x}≫\\operatorname{ln}⁡x$ for large values of $x,$ the numerator is growing much faster than the denominator. Consequently, we conclude that\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{{e}^{x}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}=\\infty .\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to \\infty }(\\frac{{e}^{x}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}+2)=\\infty .\n$$" "Both the numerator and denominator approach $\\infty $ as $x\\to \\infty .$ However, since ${e}^{x}≫\\operatorname{ln}⁡x$ for large values of $x,$ the numerator is growing much faster than the denominator. Consequently, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\lim_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{{e}^{x}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}=\\infty .\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\lim_{x\\to \\infty }(\\frac{{e}^{x}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}+2)=\\infty .\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186314719 :question/problem "Evaluate the following limit:\n\n${lim}_{x\\to \\infty }(\\frac{{e}^{x/4}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+1)}-2)=$\n{{field-1}}" "Evaluate the following limit:\n\n$\\lim_{x\\to \\infty }(\\frac{{e}^{x/4}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+1)}-2)=$\n{{field-1}}"] [:db/cas 17592186314719 :question/worked-solution "Both the numerator and denominator approach $\\infty $ as $x\\to \\infty .$ However, since ${e}^{x/4}≫\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+1)$ for large values of $x,$ the numerator is growing much faster than the denominator. Consequently, we conclude that\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{{e}^{x/4}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+1)}=\\infty .\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to \\infty }(\\frac{{e}^{x/4}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+1)}-2)=\\infty .\n$$" "Both the numerator and denominator approach $\\infty $ as $x\\to \\infty .$ However, since ${e}^{x/4}≫\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+1)$ for large values of $x,$ the numerator is growing much faster than the denominator. Consequently, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\lim_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{{e}^{x/4}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+1)}=\\infty .\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\lim_{x\\to \\infty }(\\frac{{e}^{x/4}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+1)}-2)=\\infty .\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186314739 :question/problem "Evaluate the following limit:\n\n${lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{x}=$\n{{field-1}}" "Evaluate the following limit:\n\n$$\n\\lim_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{x}=\n$$\n{{field-1}}"] [:db/cas 17592186314739 :question/worked-solution "The numerator here is a bounded, oscillating function with \n\n$$\n|\\operatorname{sin}⁡x|\\le 1.\n$$\n\nHowever, the denominator $x$ grows without bound as $x\\to \\infty .$ Since the denominator grows much faster than the (bounded) numerator, we conclude that\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{x}=0.\n$$\n\nWe can see this from the graph of $y=\\frac