what is $\\lim_{x\\to -\\infty }\\frac{p(x)}{q(x)}?$"] [:db/cas 17592186335942 :question/worked-solution "To compute ${lim}_{x\\to \\,1}f(x),$ we must compute the left and right-sided limits separately.\n\nHowever, the left-sided limit ${lim}_{x\\to \\,{1}^{-}}f(x)$ does not exist since $f(x)$ is not defined on the interval $x\\in (-1,1).$ \n\nConsequently, the overall limit does not exist either:\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to 1}f(x)=\\text{DNE}.\n$$" "To compute $\\lim_{x\\to \\,1}f(x),$ we must compute the left and right-sided limits separately.\n\nHowever, the left-sided limit $\\lim_{x\\to \\,{1}^{-}}f(x)$ does not exist since $f(x)$ is not defined on the interval $x\\in (-1,1).$ \n\nConsequently, the overall limit does not exist either:\n\n$$\n\\lim_{x\\to 1}f(x)=\\text{DNE}.\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186335943 :question/problem "Calculate ${lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\,\\,\\frac{3{x}^{4}+2}{{x}^{3}-7x}.$" "Calculate $\\lim_{x\\to \\infty }\\,\\,\\frac{3{x}^{4}+2}{{x}^{3}-7x}.$"] [:db/cas 17592186335944 :question/problem "Calculate ${lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\,\\,\\frac{{x}^{3}+x}{2{x}^{2}+x+4}.$" "Calculate $\\lim_{x\\to \\infty }\\,\\,\\frac{{x}^{3}+x}{2{x}^{2}+x+4}.$"] [:db/cas 17592186335945 :question/problem "Calculate ${lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }\\,\\,\\frac{4{x}^{5}-9}{{x}^{3}+8x}.$" "Calculate $\\lim_{x\\to -\\infty }\\,\\,\\frac{4{x}^{5}-9}{{x}^{3}+8x}.$"] [:db/cas 17592186335949 :question/problem "Evaluate ${lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{{e}^{x}}{{x}^{5}}.$" "Evaluate $\\lim_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{{e}^{x}}{{x}^{5}}.$"] [:db/cas 17592186335949 :question/worked-solution "Both the numerator and denominator approach $\\infty $ as $x\\to \\infty .$ However, since ${e}^{x}≫{x}^{5}$ for large values of $x,$ the numerator is growing much faster than the denominator. Consequently, we conclude that\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{{e}^{x}}{{x}^{5}}=\\infty .\n$$" "Both the numerator and denominator approach $\\infty $ as $x\\to \\infty .$ However, since ${e}^{x}≫{x}^{5}$ for large values